{"kind":"artifact","text":"The MCP status reference describes the lanes the tool actually returns, at the rebased head. It says the lanes hold work still owed, that a satisfied or withdrawn commitment is finished and ordinary reasoning staleness under it does not reopen it, and why: that staleness blocks nothing and reaches most closed commitments, so a lane full of it hid the rows still owed. It points at totals.stale_commitments for the per-status count and at work with stale=include for the records themselves, and states that each listed row still carries its own stale field. The totals row of the field table names the artifact counts split into stale, retired and superseded-world. The rebase conflicted here with the #6356 paragraph about lane rows carrying conditions, report_status, reported_head and latest_review; both paragraphs were kept because they answer different questions — one says what a row carries, the other says which rows appear — and neither contradicts the other. Tests passed: go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 uncached and go test ./... -count=1 exit 0.","body":{"branch":"request/staleness-presentation","commit":"0ff186ec952ee84dda6fadeeb04ea9316b0aec24","head":"0ff186ec952ee84dda6fadeeb04ea9316b0aec24","path":"docs/reference/mcp/status.md"}}